From 00cef47d228d12ae501b655c32f5167819e97531 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Starwey <moonbite233@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:37:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netpoll: synchronize pre-existing NAPI polls before enabling
 console

Backport upstream 2da4def0f487f24bbb0cece3bb2bcdcb918a0b72
(stable c0e32ec90a9ab3d64268c57ddf631cd0d3eb0e5d).
The SDK setup function uses the older put/error path and a device tracker;
retain that code and add the same RCU grace period after rtnl_unlock.

This prevents an existing normal NAPI poll from overlapping the first
netpoll poll while dev->npinfo becomes visible. It repairs the diagnostic
netconsole path; it is not claimed to fix the camera/MPP hang.

Link: https://github.com/gregkh/linux/commit/c0e32ec90a9ab3d64268c57ddf631cd0d3eb0e5d
---
 net/core/netpoll.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/core/netpoll.c b/net/core/netpoll.c
index 657abbb7d..89f5358d7 100644
--- a/net/core/netpoll.c
+++ b/net/core/netpoll.c
@@ -800,6 +800,13 @@ int netpoll_setup(struct netpoll *np)
 		goto put;
 	netdev_tracker_alloc(ndev, &np->dev_tracker, GFP_KERNEL);
 	rtnl_unlock();
+
+	/* Make sure all NAPI polls which started before dev->npinfo
+	 * was visible have exited before we start calling NAPI poll.
+	 * NAPI skips locking if dev->npinfo is NULL.
+	 */
+	synchronize_rcu();
+
 	return 0;
 
 put:
